node_modules
*.tsbuildinfo

# lib/ is committed on purpose. The dshfind registry inspects the public
# source tree and requires the manifest's `main` to be a file that is actually
# in the repository — build output that only exists after `npm run build` fails
# its check with `missing_file`. Rebuild and commit it with any source change,
# or the registry serves different code than npm does.

# Claude Code worktrees and local session state live inside the repo.
.claude

# Packed artifacts from npm pack / the package check.
*.tgz

# Scratch code maps; kept maps live in docs/whiteboards.
.exdraw
